<title>FRANCE: Paris June 97 import traffic up 0.7 pct  - ADP.</title>
<headline>Paris June 97 import traffic up 0.7 pct  - ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>June 1997 import airfreight traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 42,941 tonnes, an increase of 4.1 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The Paris airports June 1997 import traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on June 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>    Domestic		2,054  down 17.7</p>
<p>    European Union	6,477    up 22.1</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe	 1,045    up 11.7</p>
<p>    North Africa	    566    up 23.6</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa  3,662  down 15.2</p>
<p>    North America	15,020  down  5.6</p>
<p>    French territories    747    up  1.2</p>
<p>    Latin America	 1,492  down  8.8</p>
<p>    Middle East	   1,870  down  5.0</p>
<p>    Far East	     10,008    up 12.8</p>
<p>    Total		  42,941    up  0.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
